a4's probe frame. A REAL habitat render at run resolution, shipped with the gate.

  source     /DATA/FOUND/runs/20260826_112549_hm3d_00861/room_frames/
             room_0@1787736474.679392067.jpg
  copied     2026-08-31, archive read-only (rule 12)
  sha256_16  e3e009c51ead2dad
  size       74175 bytes, 640x480 RGB

WHY A FILE AND NOT np.zeros((64,64,3)):
a4 sent a 64x64 zero frame for its three calls. The Modal service takes a different code path
for a degenerate input: it returned timing keys ['total','yolo_world'] for that frame and
['detector','sam2','total'] for this one, from the same endpoint, minutes apart. So a4 was
asserting a contract against an input no run ever sends, and it refused run 16 for a reason
that did not describe the run. The same defect could as easily have produced a false PASS.

WHY SHIPPED AND NOT READ FROM A BUNDLE:
a gate that reads the archive asserts whatever the archive has become. This frame is fixed, so
what a4 asserts does not change when the corpus does.

WHY 640x480 AND NOT SMALLER:
that is the resolution runs send. Shrinking it risks re-entering the degenerate path this file
exists to leave.
